KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ specialization: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ __is_same: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ u8 string literal: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [basic.fundamental]/9, [lex.string]/6: char8_t is a distinct type
with underlying type unsigned char, and u8"a" has type const char8_t[2].
The front end treats char8_t as unsigned char (parse.cpp), and
c_preprocess.cpp undefines __cpp_char8_t so that the library does not
declare duplicate specializations; kind<unsigned char> then selects
kind<char8_t>.  cpp11_specialization_distinguishes_fundamental_types
covers the other character types.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this
program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
